 B-roll:** Interweave quick cuts of aspirational, relevant imagery (e.g., nature, healthy activities, abstract representations of focus/joy) to illustrate concepts without distracting from the core message.\n- **Consistent Brand Palette:** Employ a curated color palette that evokes both credibility (e.g., blues, whites) and positive energy/insight (e.g., yellows, bright greens).\n\n## 4. Psychology (Neuro-Code)\n- **Curiosity Gap & Revelation:** The \"Can you REALLY...?\" question, combined with \"hidden switch\" and \"hack\" language, creates an irresistible curiosity gap, promising a novel, exclusive insight and triggering a dopamine rush upon its \"reveal.\"\n- **Empowerment & Self-Efficacy:** Offering \"hacks\" and \"switches\" directly appeals to the human desire for control and agency over one's own body and mind, fostering a sense of capability and hope.\n- **Problem-Solution & Immediate Gratification:** Directly addresses a universal desire (happiness/well-being) with clear, actionable steps, satisfying the brain's craving for efficient solutions and potential quick wins.\n- **Credibility & Authority (Subtle):** Leveraging terms like \"hormones,\" \"psychology,\" and scientific visuals provides an underlying layer of trustworthiness, satisfying the brain's need for reliable, evidence-based information.\n- **Simplification of Complexity:** Breaking down complex biological or psychological processes into digestible \"hacks\" or \"switches\" makes daunting topics feel achievable and less intimidating, encouraging engagement and retention.",
